  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "APPEND\n\nA list is a pair:\n\n  [ first, the rest ]\n\nand a box with NO holes is\nthe empty list. Here\n\n  [1,[2,[]]]  and  [3,[4,[]]]\n\ngo in, and 1,2,3,4 comes\nback -- one link at a time,\neach carrying a promise of\nthe next."
   },
   "x": -1.05,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "TO RUN IT\n\nGive the three-hole box to\nthe FinishAppend robot.\n\nIt stops by itself when the\nlists run out.\n\nEach link lands inside the\npromise the last one carried,\nso the answer grows on the\nnest marked \"both lists\"\nfrom the outside in."
   },
   "x": -0.35,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "BOTH FORMS AT ONCE\n\nThe house reads the answer as\nit arrives and builds the same\nthing as a flat box.\n\nA list is easy to BUILD one\nlink at a time and hard to\nREAD: [1,[2,[3,[]]]] is a box\nholding a nest holding a box,\nthree deep. A box with three\nholes you can take in at a\nglance.\n\nIt never touches the original.\nIts nest is a twin of the\nanswer nest -- one nest in two\nplaces -- so both fill link by\nlink, side by side."
   },
   "x": 0.55,
   "z": 2.6
  }
